1
00:00:00,033 --> 00:00:04,433
Weekend Gap Guard: a pre-trade risk gate for tokenized stocks on BNB Chain.

2
00:00:04,467 --> 00:00:12,333
From Friday 16:00 to Monday 09:30 New York time the stock market prints nothing. Ondo, xStocks and bStocks tokens keep trading on BSC.

3
00:00:12,333 --> 00:00:20,100
A stop-loss cannot fill at a price the market never prints. The guard answers every order with ALLOW, REDUCE or BLOCK, and says why.

4
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:26,033
All numbers come from real BSC data pulled from the public Binance Wallet endpoints, with no API key.

5
00:00:27,033 --> 00:00:36,567
A real weekend, hour by hour: TSLA from all three issuers. The dashed line is Friday's close, the frozen reference; red and amber strips are the guard's verdicts.

6
00:00:36,567 --> 00:00:40,867
Friday, market open: the stop can fill, so a 2,000 dollar buy is allowed.

7
00:00:40,867 --> 00:00:45,733
Last hour before the close: you are about to carry weekend risk. The cap is halved.

8
00:00:45,733 --> 00:00:51,267
Saturday: risk is priced on the weekend gap, 9.6% here, not on the 3% stop. 2,000 becomes 875.

9
00:00:51,267 --> 00:00:56,900
The xStocks pool for TSLA on BSC had not traded for hours: no live mark, so the guard blocks it.

10
00:00:57,700 --> 00:01:03,167
MSTR, the largest Monday gap in our record: +8.9%. The token climbs into Monday's pre-open...

11
00:01:03,167 --> 00:01:09,233
...and once the weekend drift passes one sigma of a weekend move, the cap is halved again: 625 dollars.

12
00:01:10,233 --> 00:01:20,167
The live board, recorded from the public endpoints: Ondo and bStocks agree within 0.15%. Most xStocks pools on BSC are stale or up to 20% off the stock, and are blocked.

13
00:01:21,167 --> 00:01:26,233
Out of sample, no Monday gap in 540 ticker-weekends exceeded the guard's 99% estimate.

14
00:01:26,233 --> 00:01:32,867
Saturday buys of 5,000 dollars over 129 real weekends: worst Monday loss minus 218 dollars raw, minus 38 guarded.

15
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:38,600
The same engine runs as a CLI and as an Agent Skill. This is a live call to the public endpoints.

16
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:43,767
It hands the allowed size to the Binance Agentic Wallet as a quote, with a slippage cap.

17
00:01:43,767 --> 00:01:52,167
Checked against the real baw 1.10.0 CLI: the command parses and stops at sign-in. Signing needs a Binance account, so the guard never executes.

18
00:01:52,167 --> 00:01:55,433
Everything is tested offline.

19
00:01:55,467 --> 00:02:00,467
Weekend Gap Guard: size tokenized-stock trades for the market that is actually open.
